    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nLocated in the heart of Doonbeg village, this three-bedroom semi-detached home is within walking distance of all village amenities. Built in 2001 and extending to approximately 114.4 sq. mt. the property occupies a corner position on the front row of the development with off-street parking to the front and gated side access to a fully enclosed, south-facing rear garden.\n\nThe ground floor accommodation comprises of an entrance hallway, a generous main reception room with fireplace and sliding patio doors to the rear garden, a spacious kitchen/dining room and separate utility. Upstairs are three bedrooms, all with built-in wardrobes, and one boasting an en-suite, finishing off the upstairs accommodation is a fully tiled main bathroom. The property benefits from electric heating, mains water and mains sewage.\n\nDoonbeg is a popular village on the West Clare coast offering a range of everyday amenities and is ideally positioned for enjoying the West Clare coastline, with White Strand approximately five minutes away and the beaches at Kilkee and Doughmore within a ten-minute drive.\n\nWith its village centre setting, south-facing rear garden and excellent access to the surrounding coastline, this property would make an ideal permanent residence, first-time buyer home or investment property with viewing highly recommended and strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents. PSL 002295."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 4m x 1.4m\nTile flooring, side aspect window, carpeted stairs leading to first floor landing and doors to main reception and kitchen dining.\n\nMain Reception - 6.6m x 3.75m\nTimber flooring, front aspect window, rear sliding glass patio door, recess ceiling lighting, tv point, timber surround fireplace with cast iron inset and polished flag, door to understairs storage and open access to kitchen.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 6.6m x 3.2m\nTile flooring, dual aspect windows to the front and rear, recess ceiling lighting, built-in wall and base units with ample work surfaces, tile splash back, single drainer sink, integrated extractor hood and fan, space for cooker and under counter fridge, space and plumbing for dishwasher and door to utility.\n\nUtility Room - 2.7m x 2m\nTile flooring, rear aspect window, rear door access, built-in units with counter top space and space and plumbing for washing machine and dryer.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 3m x 2m\nTimber style flooring, rear aspect window, door to hotpress housing immersion tank and storage and doors to all three bedrooms and main bathroom.\n\nBedroom One - 3.75m x 3.2m\nTimber style flooring, front aspect window, built-in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and storage.\n\nMain Bathroom - 2.65m x 2.15m\n* Size includes hotpress spaceFully tiled ceiling to floor, rear aspect window, low level wc, wash hand basin with overhead wall mounted mirror and light, corner fitted bath unit with overhead shower attachment.\n\nBedroom Two En-Suite - 3.7m x 3.5m\nTimber style flooring, front and side aspect windows, built-in wardrobes with ample storage and door to en-suite.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.7m x 1.2m\nFully tiled ceiling to floor, low level wc, wash hand basin with overhead mirror and light, corner fitted shower tray with overhead pump shower and glass panel shower door.\n\nBedroom Three - 2.9m x 2.75m\nTimber style flooring, rear aspect window and built-in wardrobes with ample storage.\n\nOutside - \nFront - Open tarmac drive, off street parking, raised beds with pea gravel and mature shrubs and gated side access to the rear.Rear - Low maintenance, fully enclosed garden, block wall boundaries to the sides and rear, cut stone paved area and mature trees and shrubs.\n\n"
      },
      {
